@startbpmn BP16_ConsultTheAdvisor
lang en

output L1 "01_detailed/BP16_ConsultTheAdvisor.bpmn"
output L2 "02_detailed/BP16_ConsultTheAdvisor.bpmn"

' Provenance (never in a drawn note, lint rule 5):
'   - the advisor is an off-system actor, so it is a BLACK-BOX pool: messages cross its boundary
'     and nothing of its working is drawn, which is also what Intent section 5 types it as:
'     BR-66, SA 2026-10-11
'   - one advisor, available anywhere, aware of where the user is, never blocking: BR-66
'   - one conversation per session, cleared deliberately: BR-66
'   - the advisor sees the whole funnel, plus vision and mission when set: BR-67
'   - a proposal is a structured typed object, never prose to be parsed: BR-68
'   - applying writes immediately and completely; a creation proposal carries everything: BR-69
'   - at most one outstanding proposal per target; a revision supersedes its predecessor: BR-70
'   - ONE PROPOSAL PER ACT. Applying and dismissing each act on the one proposal the user picked:
'     there is no apply-the-whole-answer and no dismiss-the-whole-answer, which is what the
'     no-multi-select rule says everywhere else in the product anyway. BR-71, the one rule that let
'     a gesture act on several at once, is retired with them: BR-70, BR-85, ~~BR-71~~,
'     SA 2026-10-18 ("I changed it to what I want")
'   - the advisor acts only through the operations the user has, deletions included: BR-72
'   - an applied operation discloses and asks exactly what it would for the user: BR-72
'   - so applying is a disclosure and a write, never one call that asks and acts: BR-12, BR-72
'   - and the two gestures are the REQUEST and the ACT, never two confirmations: accepting a
'     proposal is what asks what applying it would take, the gateway is the one decision, and the
'     step on its approve branch commits by doing the thing - named for the act, as every
'     committing step is: BR-72, DRW-26, DRW-28, SA 2026-10-18 ("it requires a decision and another
'     confirmation afterwards?!")
'   - a proposal may land where the user is not working, and saying so is part of applying: BR-74
'   - it never silently fails and never hands over an inert proposal: BR-75
'   - so the call can FAIL and the drawing says so: an unreachable service, a timeout, or an
'     answer nothing usable could be made of is reported as what it is, by the one answer that
'     carries the proposals when there are any. No retry arrow is drawn: a request worth repeating
'     is the whole gesture started again, not a loop back into the pending one: BR-66, BR-75,
'     G-4, SA 2026-10-16
'   - the user's words are a REQUEST, and what the system submits to the service is the
'     CONVERSATION it belongs to - so the exchange is kept by the act that sends it, and the panel
'     reads it back with its outstanding proposals: BR-66, SA 2026-10-16
'   - an apply that fails is NOT this: applying runs the user's own operation, and a write that
'     cannot be verified is rejected with its reason by the system, which is BR-128's and is
'     drawn in no process: BR-69, BR-72, BR-128
'   - the panel comes current on its own; higher latency than everything else is accepted: BR-118
'   - the conversation is journaled but not version-controlled: section 3
'   - unfinished input is a draft, forms included: the field drafts as it is filled in, and the
'     operation that keeps it is drawn ONCE, in BP19, not per editing process. Here it is a
'     bound rule on the step that fills the field: BR-121, SA 2026-10-11
'   - NOTHING IS FETCHED HERE. Every record is loaded once, at start-up (BP01), so a step that only
'     went to the store is gone, and one that selects or qualifies what the act works on says so
'     instead of saying read. What a chain still asks the system for is what it COMPUTES, which is
'     business and stays out of the client. When data is read is a detail design decision:
'     BR-128, DRW-14, SA 2026-10-17 ("when we will read data is not a business concern, but a
'     detail design decision ... I rule that this will be done once at startup")
'     Call site BP16.01 (Open the advisor conversation) is RETIRED with the fetch it was, its id never
'     reused: the session's conversation and the view the user is on are both in play, so opening the
'     panel asks the system for nothing: ADR-066, SA 2026-10-17
'   - OPENING THE PANEL IS NOT DRAWN. It asks the system for nothing and decides nothing - the panel
'     splits the active tab, knows which view and which selection the user is on, and suspends
'     nothing - so it is the surface's own business and no act of this process: the drawing starts
'     on the hub, as every other hub process does: BR-66, BR-118, DRW-02,
'     SA 2026-10-18 ("'Open the advisor panel' is a UI-only action, no business relevance")
'   - THE CONVERSATION IS KEPT so that it can be sent as context with every later request: each turn
'     is added to it, the ask's own and the answer that comes back, and that is what carries the
'     exchange across turns. It is journaled and not version-controlled (section 3), and the panel
'     reads it back with its outstanding proposals: BR-66, BR-67, SA 2026-10-17,
'     SA 2026-10-18 ("To store the conversation, so that we can serve it as context for future
'     requests?" - yes, and the steps now say so)
'
' Scope: this process is the conversation and the proposals. The writes a proposal causes are the
' user's own operations, drawn in whichever process owns the entity, so they are reached through
' this process rather than redrawn in it.
'
' Call-site collapsing: nothing collapses into applying or dismissing any more - each acts on the
' one proposal the user picked (SA 2026-10-18). The ten catalog types are the
' payload of a proposal, not ten operations.

pool "User" {
  start "A second opinion wanted"
  :Work with the advisor;
  rule BR-118
  if "What needs doing?" then "ask something"
    :Write the request;
    rule BR-121
    :Submit the request;
    send "Ask the advisor" to askIn
    receive "The answer, or what went wrong" as answer
    note "The answer arrives on its own. The advisor is slower than the rest of the product and stays non-blocking while it thinks. An unreachable service, a timeout, or an answer nothing usable could be made of is reported as what it is, and nothing is left looking like a proposal."
    if "Did the advisor answer?" rule BR-75 then "it answered"
      end "The advisor answered"
    else "it did not"
      end "Nothing usable came back"
    endif

  elseif "What needs doing?" then "take a proposal up"
    :Accept the proposal;
    send "See what applying will take" to applyImpactIn
    receive "What applying will take, and where it lands" as applyImpact
    note "Applying runs the user's own operation, so whatever that operation discloses is disclosed here: what a deletion will take, the answers an archiving offers, and any part of the funnel the change lands in."
    if "Approve what applying takes?" rule BR-72 then "approve"
      :Apply the proposal;
      send "Apply the proposal" to applyIn
      receive "What was applied, and where" as applied
      note "The proposal is written completely. Nothing is half-applied."
    else "reject"
      :Abandon the application;
      note "The proposal stays outstanding and nothing is written."
    endif
    end "Proposal settled"

  elseif "What needs doing?" then "turn one down"
    :Dismiss the proposal;
    send "Dismiss the proposal" to dismissIn
    receive "What was dismissed" as dismissed
    end "Proposal dismissed"

  elseif "What needs doing?" then "start over"
    :Clear the conversation;
    send "Clear the conversation" to clearIn
    receive "What was cleared" as cleared
    note "Clearing is deliberate. One conversation runs for the session and nothing clears it on the user's behalf."
    end "Conversation cleared"

  endif
}

system pool "Bearing" {
  messageStart "Request submitted" as askIn
  call "BP16.02_AskTheAdvisor" "Ask the advisor" {
    :Submit the request incl. the conversation and current state;
    rule BR-67
    :Extend conversation by request;
    rule BR-66
  }
  send "Advice requested" to "Advisor"
  note "The whole funnel goes with the request: themes, ideas, goals, routines, focus history, tasks and progress check-ins."
  end "Request sent"

  receive "Advisor answered" from "Advisor"
  call "BP16.03_TakeTheAdvisorsAnswer" "Take the advisor's answer" {
    :Turn each actionable part of the answer into a typed proposal;
    rule BR-68
    :Keep what could not be turned into one as prose, and say so;
    rule BR-75
    :Supersede the outstanding proposal on each target the answer touches;
    rule BR-70
    :Keep the answer with the conversation, for the turns that follow;
    rule BR-66
    :Report the outcome;
    rule BR-75
    rule BR-118
  }
  send "The answer, or what went wrong" to answer
  note "A proposal is a structured object, never prose to be parsed. At most one proposal is outstanding per target, and an already-applied or already-dismissed one is closed and untouched."
  end "Answer answered"

  messageStart "Application impact requested" as applyImpactIn
  call "BP16.07_ReadWhatApplyingWillTake" "See what applying will take" {
    :Report what applying will take;
    rule BR-72
    rule BR-117
    rule BR-74
  }
  send "What applying will take, and where it lands" to applyImpact
  note "A proposal that takes nothing has nothing to disclose. One that deletes or archives discloses exactly what the user's own gesture would, because it is that gesture."
  end "Application impact answered"

  messageStart "Application requested" as applyIn
  call "BP16.04_ApplyTheProposal" "Apply the proposal" {
    :Apply the proposal;
    rule BR-72
    rule BR-69
    rule BR-70
    :Report what was applied, and where it landed;
    rule BR-74
  }
  send "What was applied, and where" to applied
  note "A proposal to create something carries everything that thing needs."
  end "Application answered"

  messageStart "Dismissal requested" as dismissIn
  call "BP16.05_DismissTheProposal" "Dismiss the proposal" {
    :Close the proposal as dismissed;
    rule BR-70
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "What was dismissed" to dismissed
  note "A proposal already applied or dismissed is closed, and nothing reopens it (BR-70)."
  end "Dismissal answered"

  messageStart "Clear requested" as clearIn
  call "BP16.06_ClearTheConversation" "Clear the conversation" {
    :Drop the conversation and its outstanding proposals;
    rule BR-66
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "What was cleared" to cleared
  note "Applied and dismissed proposals are closed already and are unaffected by clearing."
  end "Clear answered"
}

blackbox pool "Advisor"

@endbpmn
